{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1089298-insatiable-s-moments-a-brief-list-of-ideas","id":1089298,"title":"Insatiable's Moments: A brief list of ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T12:02:08-07:00","id":1089298,"title":"Insatiable's Moments: A brief list of ideas","content":"I've been thinking about Insatiables and, at least for me, to associate a concept with a Moment is not always as easy as I'd like it to be. So, I wrote down all the Moments and essentially did a little brainstorming about all the associations I give to each of them. It's nothing innovative or genial and, as the book says, the various Moments intentionally overlap when it comes to concepts and narrative associations, but I found it an useful exercise and thought that perhaps it was worth sharing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clashing Faults: </b>earthquakes, avalanches, volcanoes. suffocation, being crushed, being trapped, brutality, lack of emotions, authority, strength, resolve, composure, insignificance, domination, hunger for power, imposingness, being forced to hide, fear of being weak<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Freezing Hell:</b> blizzards, storms, tornadoes, being flayed, being exposed, starving, callousness, viciousness, hate, envy, loneliness, stamina, dexterity, resolve, hunger for warmth, patience, cruelty, obsessions, lack of something, being forced to kill, fear of missing something<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Molten Earth:</b> volcanoes, wildfire, lava, burning alive, being reduced to ash, succumbing to emotions, losing control, rage, impulse, strength, presence, hunger for destruction, recklessness, shows of power, inhabitable locations, forced renewal, being forced to leave, fear of dying,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Primordial Seas: </b>oceans, tsunami, maelstrom, storms, floods, drowning, being overwhelmed, being overpowered, restlessness, superiority, sacrifice, abominable lifeforms, birth strength, wits, resolve, being stronger than others, being better than others, evolution, mutations, fear of being eaten<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Void: </b>cosmic phenomena, black holes, meteors, supernova, laws of reality, stars, sudden death, arrogance, death without a reason, threats from distant places, unknown, certain doom, intelligence, presence, insignificance, madness, mind-breaking revelations, alien morality, abominable lifeforms, being out of place, being unable to understand, fear of being meaningless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:10:02-07:00","id":1089301,"title":"","content":"Some ideas of my own:<br /> <b>Clashing Faults:</b> The meteorite strike that likely killed the dinosaurs.<br /> <b>Freezing Hell:</b> The very first extinction-level event on Earth; the moon.<br /> <b>Molten Earth:</b> A gamma ray burster; the sun...to be specific, the sun as a bringer of cancer.<br /> <b>Primordial Seas:</b> The earliest epochs of multicellular lifeforms.<br /> <b>Void:</b> Non-existence; various kinds of dead stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:25:41-07:00","id":1089623,"title":"","content":"I was working on an Insatiable brood and here are the notes I took:<ul><li>Insatiable (Primordial Seas, Tyrant): Coatlicue (Mother of Insatiables) and her children:</li> </ul>Clashing Faults (Physical, Collector): The giant worm<br /> Freezing Hell (Physical, Tyrant): The glacier<br /> Molten Earth (Social, Tyrant): The burning star<br /> Void (Social, Collector): The doomsday clock<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:25:54-07:00","id":1089959,"title":"","content":"I would honestly approach the question from the perspective of the almost unrecognizable human half of the Insatiables themselves. <br /> <br /> For instance, let's look at everyone's favorite internet predator: Null Snyper. Just like a Begotten she has a Legend, Life, Hunger, and Moment that represent both her Nightmarish half and her human half. Even though like all Insatiables her Legend tends to dominate her human half, her Life still defines the shape of her powers and hungers. Otherwise she would go around hunting prey to break both physically and mentally before devouring them like most of the other Insatiable Tyrants do. Instead, her hunt and her powers reinforce her Life's prefered method of domination: the Internet. <br /> <br /> So, her Moment takes the form of hostile cyber space where victims are metaphorically stripped away of hope and oxygen by the cold and pitiless void until they explosive decompress...metaphorically. Like the Horror, the Moment cares only to feed it's insatiable hunger. Null Snyper's malice and hatred comes from the person she was before the transformation, and the person she is now that she too has an insatiable hunger and otherworldly powers. <br /> <br /> So, what ideas and concepts are reflected by the Insatiable's human halfs? And how can those be used in the Chronicles to make engaging, and sometimes sympathetic, antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 05-08-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:54:19-07:00","id":1089980,"title":"","content":"Oh, by all means. My little scheme does not work at all if you take the Moments in a vacuum without considering the human half concept.<br /> <br /> It's way less pretentious than it looks, merely a list of mental associations for the Moments. Indeed, I agree completely with your approach: find the character first, then look at what kind of ideas and themes the human half has and reflects, then pick a Moment (and Horrific Form) that seems fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:35:27-07:00","id":1090003,"title":"","content":"Oooh, well that's actually my bad. Made an assumption there and it was untrue. <br /> <br /> In light of that, your list is sound and comprehensive. Can't think of anything else to add off the top of my head really, we'd need a little bit more information about the Moments and the Insatiable as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T16:08:14-07:00","id":1090018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1089298-insatiable-s-moments-a-brief-list-of-ideas?p=1090003#post1090003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh, well that's actually my bad. Made an assumption there and it was untrue.<br /> <br /> In light of that, your list is sound and comprehensive. Can't think of anything else to add off the top of my head really, we'd need a little bit more information about the Moments and the Insatiable as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>No harm done, should have explained myself better. As for more Insatiables, my guess is we'll have to wait until the Storyteller's Guide","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T16:36:11-07:00","id":1090025,"title":"","content":"Tying the moments into more primal/animal fears:<br /> <br /> Clashing Faults- you must survive, but you are trapped. Wherever you go, you never find home, only more caves, more tunnels, more darkness. You can never escape.<br /> <br /> Frozen Hell- you must survive, but you are alone. The resources you relied on are gone, your pack is gone, the world you're adapted to is gone. Nothing can save you.<br /> <br /> Molten Earth- you must survive, but nowhere is safe. It's all fire, and poison, and pain, and death. There is no place to hide.<br /> <br /> Primordial Seas- you must survive, but you are being hunted. It is bigger then you, faster, stronger. It will eat you, and you cannot stop it.<br /> <br /> The Void- you must survive, but you do not belong here. There is no food, no water, no air, no earth. Something like you can never survive out here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}